  "visualBrief": "Individual San Thome Basilica, Chennai: white Gothic nave with triple pointed west portals/upper windows and gable, tall west-south offset tower with stepped pointed fields, octagonal upper stage and long white faceted needle/cross, smaller crossing spire, red tiled roofs, tall transept and three eastern fingers/chapels. Repeated stepped buttresses/pinnacles and two tiers of pointed side fields. Four budgeted browser levels, shared plaster/limestone/tile/wood, linear tints and metric UVs. Standard terrain foundations. Exact statues/reliefs/inscriptions, carved/parapet tracery, stained-glass artwork, full interior/crypt, liturgical column, flags, fences/palms/parking, adjoining town, surveyed paving/thresholds and walking excluded.",
